course: dictionary
lesson: 13889
title: Kwa: a word with many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Kwa is a word you may meet in three different ways: as the name of a family of languages, as a little Swahili word, or as a short sound. The clues in the sentence show you which one it is.
explain: «The Kwa languages are spoken in West Africa, in countries such as Ghana and Nigeria.» Here kwa is part of a name for a group of languages. Akan, Ewe and Fon are all Kwa languages.
explain: «Kwa heri, Amina!» is Swahili for goodbye. In Swahili, kwa can mean «for», «to», «with» or «by», so it often sits inside a phrase rather than standing alone.
explain: In an English story, kwa on its own is not a normal word. It may be a sound, like a duck's call, or part of a longer word. If you are not sure, check the sentence around it and look it up.
fact: Kwa is a noun when it names a large family of languages spoken in West Africa.
fact: Countries with Kwa languages include Ghana, Togo, Benin, Côte d'Ivoire and Nigeria.
fact: Akan (Twi), Ewe and Fon are all Kwa languages.
fact: In Swahili, «kwa» means «for», «to», «with» or «by», as in «kwa heri» (goodbye).
fact: As a fragment, kwa may be part of a longer word or a sound effect; it is not an English word.
exercise: «The Kwa languages are spoken in West Africa.» What does Kwa name in this sentence? | A country in Europe | *A family of languages | A river in West Africa | A type of food
exercise: In Swahili, «kwa heri» means what? | Hello | Good night | *Goodbye | Thank you
exercise: Which of these is a Kwa language? | *Ewe | French | English | Swahili
test: Where are the Kwa languages spoken? | South America | Central Asia | Northern Europe | *West Africa
test: You read «kwa» alone in an English story. What is the best first thought? | It is a Scottish word meaning grey | It is always the name of a country | It is an ordinary English word meaning "for" | *It may be a sound, a fragment, or part of a longer word
exam: In Swahili, which of these can «kwa» mean? | Blue | *For | Snow | Quickly
